# Branding and Play policy (from DECISIONS.md, BLOCKERS.md and docs/PLAY_COMPLIANCE.md)

## Launcher label and icon
- The label comes from `@string/app_name`: **"Calculator"** (`values`, default) and
  **"Hesap Makinesi"** (`values-tr`). The recents title matches.
- The icon is **original**: navy background, light body, dark display, 3×3 keys, mint "=" key.
  - It is generated from one geometry by `tool/gen_launcher_icon.py`: adaptive fg/bg,
    monochrome (themed icons), round/legacy PNGs, and the 512 px store icon
    `docs/store_icon_512.png`.
  - Change the icon only through the script, so the vector and PNGs stay identical.
- Never copy Google/Samsung/Xiaomi calculator icons or branding. No icon hiding, no alias
  switching, no reviewer-specific behaviour.

## The vault must always be disclosed
This is required, because it is what makes a calculator-looking vault allowed under Play
Deceptive Behavior / Behavior Transparency:
- Onboarding step 2 (the calculator-entry disclosure screen + toggle)
- The ⓘ dialog in the calculator
- The store listing (TR + EN)
- Reviewer notes (App access)

The app really is a working calculator. The listing and in-app behaviour must tell the same story.

## Store listing, Data safety and reviewer notes
- Drafts live in `docs/PLAY_COMPLIANCE.md` §2–4. Keep them in sync with the features.
- Data safety: no data collected or shared. On-device only. No ads. 18+. Re-check if any SDK is
  added (billing, crash reporting, backup).
- Privacy policy: `PRIVACY.md`. It must be **hosted on HTTPS before submission**.
- Still open: real support e-mail, hosted policy URL, screenshots (first screenshot = calculator
  with the ⓘ dialog open), release signing, IAP (not in this build).

## Play policy risk (v0.2): medium–high review friction
- A `DeviceAdminReceiver` / managed-profile DPC gets stricter review (Device & Network Abuse,
  Unwanted Software, sensitive-API policies).
- "Calculator label + admin component" can look like concealment.
- Mitigations already in place:
  - real calculator and full disclosure
  - empty admin policies, self-deactivation as a main-profile admin
  - Second phone gated behind the vault and fully described
  - no new permissions, no network, no reading of other apps' data
- **Fallback (split build):** a Play flavor **without** the `secondphone` components (vault +
  calculator only), with the Second phone build distributed as a signed side-loaded APK
  (GitHub releases / F-Droid style, like Shelter). The Play title can optionally be made more
  explicit, e.g. "GizliAlan: Calculator Vault".
- **Owner decision is required before any Play submission:**
  (a) submit with full disclosure and accept review friction, or (b) use the split build.
  Nothing has been submitted anywhere. Do not submit, publish or set up Play Console.

## Closed testing (context from Google Play rules, NOT from the repo docs)
- New personal Play developer accounts must run a **closed test with at least 12 testers for
  14 consecutive days** before production access. Confirm the current numbers on Google's pages.
- Setting this up means Play Console work, so it is an owner/BLOCKER step. Do not start it yourself.
